  "rationale": "The representative error is a noun following “and the”: pears has no visible output rule for a preceding determiner, leaving it with very little probability despite the grammatical noun-phrase context. The batch also contains repeated “that was” endings, while the was root has only a very low-weight general rule. Add modest contextual support for pears after a determiner and for was after the pronoun that. These are local, reusable cues rather than claims that other continuations are impossible. A determiner can precede many nouns, and that can have other continuations, so the additions preserve alternatives. Replay examples do not show either new suffix.",
